{"source_passage_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0003-PASSAGE", "text": "Background: What is physiology?\nWhat is “physiology”?\n• Physiology is scientific study of:\n• normal conditions and activities of a living organism\n• and functions and mechanisms of body parts for maintaining survival.\n• Content of “human physiology”:\n• (1) Normal conditions of human body\n• (2) Functions of human cells, tissues, and organs for achieving normal conditions", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 1 - Human Body and Chemicals (July 2026)", "source_file": "01 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L1 (Jul 2026).pdf", "source_page_ids": ["HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0003"], "source_pages": [{"source_page_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0003", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 1 - Human Body and Chemicals (July 2026)", "source_file": "01 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L1 (Jul 2026).pdf", "page_number": 3, "page_number_type": "slide_number", "slide_number": 3, "pdf_page": 3, "formatted": "01 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L1 (Jul 2026).pdf, slide 3 (PDF p. 3)"}], "slide_number": 3, "section_ids": ["HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0003", "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-PART01", "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "HHS3190M-COURSE"], "section_path": ["HHS3190M - Human Physiology and Functional Anatomy for Rehabilitation Services", "Lecture 1 - Human Body and Chemicals (July 2026)", "Background: What is physiology?", "Background: What is physiology?"], "content_type": "slide_text", "ocr_text": null, "status": "generated_not_verified", "verification_status": "generated_not_verified"}
{"source_passage_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0004-PASSAGE", "text": "Background: What is physiology?\n• The structures and positions of human body parts are highly related to their functions!\n• Thus, learning (3) basic anatomy of each organ is essential for understanding the physiological functions!", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 1 - Human Body and Chemicals (July 2026)", "source_file": "01 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L1 (Jul 2026).pdf", "source_page_ids": ["HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0004"], "source_pages": [{"source_page_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0004", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 1 - Human Body and Chemicals (July 2026)", "source_file": "01 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L1 (Jul 2026).pdf", "page_number": 4, "page_number_type": "slide_number", "slide_number": 4, "pdf_page": 4, "formatted": "01 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L1 (Jul 2026).pdf, slide 4 (PDF p. 4)"}], "slide_number": 4, "section_ids": ["HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0004", "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-PART01", "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "HHS3190M-COURSE"], "section_path": ["HHS3190M - Human Physiology and Functional Anatomy for Rehabilitation Services", "Lecture 1 - Human Body and Chemicals (July 2026)", "Background: What is physiology?", "Background: What is physiology?"], "content_type": "slide_text", "ocr_text": null, "status": "generated_not_verified", "verification_status": "generated_not_verified"}
{"source_passage_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0005-PASSAGE", "text": "Organization of Human Body\n• The organization of the human body can be broken down into several levels, from the simplest to the most complex, namely:\n• Chemical level: different chemicals (E.g. proteins)\n• Cellular level: single cell\n• Tissue level: groups of similar cells\n• Organ level: discrete structure, which contains two or more types of tissues, for specific functions\n• Organ system level: several organs that work closely together\n• Organism level: all organ systems combined to make the whole organism", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 1 - Human Body and Chemicals (July 2026)", "source_file": "01 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L1 (Jul 2026).pdf", "source_page_ids": ["HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0005"], "source_pages": [{"source_page_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0005", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 1 - Human Body and Chemicals (July 2026)", "source_file": "01 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L1 (Jul 2026).pdf", "page_number": 5, "page_number_type": "slide_number", "slide_number": 5, "pdf_page": 5, "formatted": "01 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L1 (Jul 2026).pdf, slide 5 (PDF p. 5)"}], "slide_number": 5, "section_ids": ["HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0005", "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-PART02", "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "HHS3190M-COURSE"], "section_path": ["HHS3190M - Human Physiology and Functional Anatomy for Rehabilitation Services", "Lecture 1 - Human Body and Chemicals (July 2026)", "Organization of Human Body and Organ-System Overview", "Organization of Human Body"], "content_type": "slide_text", "ocr_text": null, "status": "generated_not_verified", "verification_status": "generated_not_verified"}
