{"source_passage_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0014-PASSAGE", "text": "Important Chemicals in Human Body\n• Polysaccharides (Complex carbohydrates)\n• Formed by combination of many monosaccharides\n• Common polysaccharides\n• Fiber (Cellulose): Polysaccharide that forms cell wall of plant cell\n• Starch: carbohydrate storage form used by plants\n• Glycogen: carbohydrate storage form used by animals\n• All 3 examples are formed by combination of many glucose molecules!\n• Human digestive system cannot break down fibers!", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 1 - Human Body and Chemicals (July 2026)", "source_file": "01 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L1 (Jul 2026).pdf", "source_page_ids": ["HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0014"], "source_pages": [{"source_page_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0014", "document_id": "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "document_title": "Lecture 1 - Human Body and Chemicals (July 2026)", "source_file": "01 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L1 (Jul 2026).pdf", "page_number": 14, "page_number_type": "slide_number", "slide_number": 14, "pdf_page": 14, "formatted": "01 - HHS3190MJ Physiology L1 (Jul 2026).pdf, slide 14 (PDF p. 14)"}], "slide_number": 14, "section_ids": ["HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-P0014", "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07-PART03", "HHS3190M-L01-PHYSIOLOGY-2026-07", "HHS3190M-COURSE"], "section_path": ["HHS3190M - Human Physiology and Functional Anatomy for Rehabilitation Services", "Lecture 1 - Human Body and Chemicals (July 2026)", "Important Chemicals in Human Body", "Important Chemicals in Human Body"], "content_type": "slide_text", "ocr_text": null, "status": "generated_not_verified", "verification_status": "generated_not_verified"}
